// Project-local Zed tasks for mzi.
//
// Points a browser at this project's background preview (see .zed/settings.json
// for why the port is per-project). The preview server is already running inside
// tinymist — this only opens a tab on it, so there is no process to clean up.
//
// The task itself is silent: reveal "never" keeps the terminal panel from
// popping open, hide "always" drops the tab as soon as it is done, and the two
// show_* flags suppress the echoed command and the exit-code summary. Nothing
// here is worth watching — it is one browser call that exits immediately.
//
// To actually debug the preview, the terminal is the wrong place anyway: the
// server lives inside tinymist, so its output is in the language server log
// (command palette -> "debug: open language server logs"). If you do want this
// task visible for a moment, flip hide to "never".
//
// stdlib `webbrowser` does the OS dispatch, wrapping the same explorer / open /
// xdg-open each platform wants. The interpreter is `python`, not `python3`: on
// Windows `python3` resolves to the Microsoft Store stub and errors out.
[
  {
    "label": "Typst: Open Preview",
    "command": "python",
    "args": ["-m", "webbrowser", "-t", "http://127.0.0.1:23635/"],
    "reveal": "never",
    "hide": "always",
    "show_summary": false,
    "show_command": false
  },
]
